WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
- All right y'all we've
reached the end of the hour,

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.273
but good news,

00:00:03.273 --> 00:00:04.810
sometimes I save the best for last.

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.301
This is, what I'm liking.

00:00:06.301 --> 00:00:09.040
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:10.250
Over the last couple of years

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.210
we've all needed little boosts of humor

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:14.580
and inspiration to get us through the day.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.020
An animator known as Coolman Coffeedan.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.400
Specializes in this.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.880
Maybe you've seen his work before.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:20.910
It's so cute.

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.400
His simple hand-drawn
animations have racked up

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.440
hundreds of millions of views.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.280
They're typically super sweet and silly

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.330
with upbeat messages.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.621
Take a look.

00:00:29.621 --> 00:00:32.170
- Hey, you wanna see a magic trick?

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:36.360
I'm gonna make something
amazing... pop out of thin air.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.267
(beeping noises)

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.517
(grunting)

00:00:41.451 --> 00:00:42.284
(laughs)

00:00:42.284 --> 00:00:43.117
Yeah.

00:00:43.117 --> 00:00:45.040
It's a mirror...

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.030
because you're the one that's amazing.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.704
And you need to remember that.

00:00:51.704 --> 00:00:52.537
(audience clapping)

00:00:52.537 --> 00:00:54.370
- Aww, he's so adorable.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.640
He's also an author, his new book,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.660
Ur Special: Advice for Humans.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:00:59.493
Is out now.

00:00:59.493 --> 00:01:01.690
Let's get Coolman Coffeedan in here.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:02.891
What's up Dan?

00:01:02.891 --> 00:01:04.259
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:01:04.259 --> 00:01:05.248
- What's up Kelly?

00:01:05.248 --> 00:01:06.280
How's it going?

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.190
Thanks for having me on.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:08.030
This is awesome.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.550
- No, thank you for joining us.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.940
So this all started by accident, right?

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:13.160
- Totally by accident.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:14.730
I was always that kid in school,

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.470
doodling on my homework and my notes.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:18.450
I was that kid,

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:19.910
you know, and people like that.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:22.230
My friends around me kind
of fell in love with these

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:24.580
characters that I would
doodle on my notes.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.630
And it wasn't until this
random summer night in 2017,

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.380
when I had this three in the morning idea.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.680
I didn't really know how to animate.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:34.730
I sketched it real
quick, and I went to bed.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:35.980
Didn't think much of it.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.020
And that video ended up
being my video called,

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:39.150
snakes have legs,

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:43.403
which has gone on to be one of
the most viral hits to date.

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:46.290
Hundreds of millions of
views around the world.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:47.620
And I was like, okay, cool.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:48.453
That works.

00:01:48.453 --> 00:01:50.490
My animation resonated with people.

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.870
And a few years later,
here we are with my book.

00:01:52.870 --> 00:01:54.140
It's pretty cool.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.920
- That is super cool, that
you're doing something you love

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:56.753
and it worked out.

00:01:56.753 --> 00:01:57.586
That's awesome.

00:01:57.586 --> 00:01:59.780
And they're simple animations,
but they have a real impact.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.050
So what kind of feedback do
you get back from people?

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:05.150
- So the messages I get from
people are super heartwarming.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.220
I was at Starbucks a few weeks ago

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.400
and the barista was a fan of my work.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.093
And she was telling me how
at the start of the pandemic,

00:02:12.093 --> 00:02:13.950
she would send these videos,

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.340
my videos back and forth with
her little, little sister,

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:19.210
because they were so like, anxiety calming

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.120
and like told you
everything was gonna be okay

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.140
during such a questionable time.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.300
And that's what my videos do,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.840
for so many people around the world.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:29.137
This just remind you that,
"Hey, you're special."

00:02:29.137 --> 00:02:29.970
"You're loved."

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.770
"You're not nearly as ugly
as you may think you are."

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:35.370
And it's a source of
positivity for so many people.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.560
And this is a dream come true.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.270
I've always wanted to
do something like this.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.103
- All right.

00:02:39.103 --> 00:02:41.421
Be sure to pick up
Coolman Coffeedan's book.

00:02:41.421 --> 00:02:43.440
Ur Special: Advice for Humans.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.308
Thank you so much.

00:02:44.308 --> 00:02:45.223
Coolman Coffeedan.

00:02:45.223 --> 00:02:46.056
(audience clapping)

00:02:46.056 --> 00:02:46.890
I'm liking your posts right now.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:47.723
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:02:47.723 --> 00:02:48.556
- [Coolman Coffedan]
Thank you for having me.

00:02:48.556 --> 00:02:49.427
Thank you.

00:02:49.427 --> 00:02:50.470
- And that's not all.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.630
Our season long partner,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.463
Pilot Pen.

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:53.857
Makers of Frixion.

00:02:53.857 --> 00:02:56.480
The go to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.670
Want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly,

00:02:58.670 --> 00:02:59.610
just like you my man.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.310
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.160
How's that sound?

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:02.993
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:03:02.993 --> 00:03:04.389
- No way...

00:03:04.389 --> 00:03:05.222
Thank you so much.

00:03:05.222 --> 00:03:06.055
What?

00:03:06.055 --> 00:03:06.888
That's crazy.

00:03:06.888 --> 00:03:07.721
Kelly, thank you.

00:03:07.721 --> 00:03:08.630
That's incredible.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:09.965
- [Kelly] Well, thank you so much.

